  "step_2": "The individual reviewed the outcomes of the lotteries and stated that they chose Lottery B because it has a 100% chance of winning, while Lottery A only has a 99% chance of winning. The individual explicitly compares the probabilities of winning (i.e., receiving a positive amount) between the two lotteries. The focus is on the probability of a favorable outcome, and the individual emphasizes the difference in these probabilities (100% vs. 99%). There is no mention of outcome amounts, expected value, or any other criterion. The justification centers on the probability of success, specifically noting that B has a higher chance of winning than A. The individual does not discuss the magnitude of the outcomes or any other decision criterion.",
  "step_3": "The information considered by the individual (99% vs. 100% chance of a favorable outcome) matches exactly with the information relevant to the decision reason. The decision reason specifies that differences in outcomes are negligible and that the lottery with the higher probability of a favorable outcome is preferred. The individual's justification directly reflects this rule: they compare the probabilities of winning and conclude that B has a higher chance (100% vs. 99%). Therefore, the individual applied the decision reason by focusing on the probability of a favorable outcome and selecting the one with the higher probability. The reasoning aligns fully with the stated rule of the decision reason.",
  "final_assessment_score": 100
}

{
